    "created_at": "2018-03-04T23:55:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-04T23:55:06Z",
    "body": "> I guess we should change Firefox given the interoperability elsewhere. Doesn't seem like Firefox interpretation is substantially better?\r\n\r\nI agree with this.\r\n\r\nI think non-Firefox's current rule is \"choose better region if the value is on a boundary\".  If the value is on the boundary of optimum region and suboptimal region, it's in optimum region. If the value is on the boundary of suboptimal region and even less good region, it's in suboptimal region.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
